  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "曲選及習作",
    "sub_ename": "SELECTION OF CHINESE CHYU WITH WRITING PRACTICES",
    "describe_ch": "本課程旨在培養學生對元代散曲的認知與創作能力，以及元代散曲與雜劇的差異：在曲牌的認識上，能清楚認知元代散曲的架構、格律、用韻，並能辨別詩詞曲之間的用韻差異。在曲學發展史上，能夠了解元曲的起源、轉變與發展，並能理解曲學發展特有的時代背景。在作家作品風格上，能認清宋末至元代的曲學風尚，以及對元代雜劇架構的理解，並能擁有賞析、創作散曲的能力。",
    "describe_eh": "This course aims to cultivate students' understanding and creative abilities in regards to the Yuan Dynasty's Sanqu (or Song, a type of Chinese poetry), as well as to understand the differences between Sanqu and Zaju (a type of Chinese drama, performed by mixing songs, narrations, and dancing). For example, in terms of knowing the name of the tunes of songs, students will gain a clear understanding of the structure, the metrical patterns, and rhyme patterns of Yuan Dynasty's Sanqu, and distinguish the differences in rhyme usage among Poetry, Ci (another type of Chinese poetry), and Sanqu. In terms of the development history of Chinese music, students will learn about the origins, changes, and developments of Yuan Dynasty's Sanqu, as well as the unique historical context of the development of the genre. In terms of the writer's style, students will recognize the trends of Song and Poetry during the end of the Song Dynasty to the Yuan Dynasty, understand the structure of Zaju during the Yuan Dynasty, and possess the ability to appreciate, analyse, and create Sanqu.",
